211 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(FODMAPs are a group of carbohydrates that can be difficult for some people to digest. The term stands for Fermentable Oligosaccharides, Disaccharides, Monosaccharides, and Polyols. These compounds are naturally found in a variety of foods, including certain fruits, vegetables, dairy products, grains, and sweeteners.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

212 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(For some individuals, FODMAPs are not fully absorbed in the small intestine. When they reach the large intestine, they can draw water into the digestive tract and are fermented by gut bacteria. This process may contribute to symptoms such as bloating, gas, abdominal discomfort, and changes in bowel habits.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

213 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(A Low FODMAP approach is a structured way to identify foods that may be contributing to digestive symptoms. It is not intended to be a lifelong restrictive diet. Instead, it helps create a more personalized eating pattern by identifying individual food triggers and supporting greater digestive comfort.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

