endobj

274 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 85 0 R/E(During this phase, foods high in FODMAPs are temporarily reduced for a limited period. The goal is to create a consistent foundation that allows individuals to observe whether symptoms improve when potential triggers are minimized.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

275 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 85 0 R/E(Why This Process Matters)/Pg 18 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

276 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 85 0 R/E(The goal of the Low FODMAP approach is not permanent restriction. By identifying personal tolerance levels, individuals can enjoy greater food variety while supporting long-term digestive comfort and confidence around eating.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

277 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 85 0 R/E(Phase 2: Reintroduction)/Pg 18 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

278 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 85 0 R/E(Foods are gradually reintroduced in a structured manner to evaluate tolerance levels. This phase helps identify which FODMAP groups may contribute to symptoms and which foods can be comfortably included in the diet.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

279 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 85 0 R/E(Phase 3: Personalization)/Pg 18 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

280 0 obj
